  "caveats": [
    "The official 99-county XLS index and all 99 retained workbooks yield 1,687 unique county-qualified President source rows that reconcile exactly by Election Day, Absentee, and Total slices to every workbook county total, the certified 99-county canvass, and statewide totals. One all-zero Dallas ABSENTEE administrative row is non-geographic, leaving 1,686 colorable source rows. The separate participation report retains 1,688 identities; the statewide one-row difference is fully accounted for by Dallas (35 workbook vs 34 participation) and Lee (20 vs 22), without treating count similarity as a crosswalk. Systematic map URL enumeration retained 52 official county PDFs; 38 bodies explicitly state a January 15, 2012 effective date, 14 are vintage-unproven, and 47 URLs redirect to the official unavailable page. The Dubuque archive supplies 35 reviewed geographic code-to-polling-place mappings plus one non-geographic absentee aggregate, but four of 210 compared Election Day candidate cells differ from the SOS workbook and no code is assigned to a polygon.",
    "The workbook field headed Precinct is preserved verbatim. Dallas includes one all-zero non-geographic ABSENTEE placeholder; Lee reports 20 polling-place labels while participation reports 22 precinct/local-unit identities.",
    "Dubuque's reviewed official county archive supplies explicit numeric codes and polling-place labels, but its code 10 Obama/Romney cells and code 41 Goode/Stein cells differ from the reconciled SOS workbook. The cause is unresolved and no misconduct inference is made.",
    "Exact normalized label overlap across source families is reported only as a diagnostic and never adopted as a geometry relationship.",
    "The earlier results-index HTTP 403 artifact is an environment-specific historical observation superseded by successful HTTP 200 acquisition of the index and all 99 workbooks.",
    "Participation total-voted/absentee values are turnout context only and are not presidential contest votes.",
    "The dated 2014 statewide ZIP remains unavailable and is not backcast. No 2015, post-2020, or 2024 geometry or identifier decision is reused.",
